{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>ברעתו</b> — when he plans to do harm to the poor, the wicked is thrust down and falls. And for the righteous there is refuge and trust in HaShem, at the time of the wicked's death. Another interpretation: and the righteous, at the time he dies, still takes refuge in his death, like Hezekiah."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:51.360634516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}